STATEMENT: >>>
Grammar to load: `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-css` (nixpkgs, 0.25.0, binding present) and `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-html` (nixpkgs, 0.23.2, binding present) — two separate grammars, paired here because both files are the same small surface (`docs/sdoc/board/`, `docs/sdoc/view/`).

Candidate items, CSS (node type, confirmed against upstream `tree-sitter/tree-sitter-css`'s `src/node-types.json`): `rule_set` (a full `selector { ... }` block), `class_selector`, `id_selector`. HTML node types were not fetched this survey and are unverified — likely candidates by analogy with other tree-sitter HTML grammars are `element` and `script_element`/`style_element`, but treat these as unconfirmed until checked against `tree-sitter/tree-sitter-html`'s own `node-types.json`.

Present in this repo today: 2 CSS files (`docs/sdoc/board/assets/{app,theme}.css`) and 2 HTML files (`docs/sdoc/board/index.html`, `docs/sdoc/view/template.html`); `index.html` is what loads the board app's JS and CSS listed under WORK-LANG-JAVASCRIPT.

Gap: 4 files combined, well under the ~10-file presence bar this survey used elsewhere, and the operator did not name CSS or HTML directly; filed as one combined entry because the survey brief pre-scoped it that way and the two files types share one small surface. HTML node types remain unverified pending a follow-up fetch of upstream's `node-types.json` if this ever gets picked up.
